# `tests/` ignored the whole directory, yet the Python suite is tracked (12
# files, each force-added). Every new test therefore had to be `git add -f`-ed
# or it silently never reached the repo -- which is how a test written
# alongside the is_gpi_anchored fix nearly shipped without its test.
# Ignore the directory's CONTENTS rather than the directory, so test sources
# are tracked by default while fixture data, output/ and real_clean/ stay out.
tests/*
!tests/*.py
!tests/*.nf
legacy/
lib/
misc/
